     (epic #11762); `tortoise.premiselabs.co` is a permanent 301 onto those paths, so a
     <loc> naming it would submit a redirect and teach a crawler that the canonical URLs
     moved. Every <loc> below is the URL that answers 200.

     ⛔ THE LEGAL SPLIT IS NOT ONE SHAPE, and the file it sits in is a trap: `/license`
     governs the PRODUCT and moved under the prefix, while `/privacy`, `/tos` and `/dpa`
     govern the BUSINESS and stay at the company ROOT (`LEGAL_AT_ROOT` in
     `functions/_middleware.ts`; #11762 settled that fork explicitly). `/tortoise/privacy`
     is a 404 — measured live 2026-11-12 — so naming it here would submit a dead URL, not
     merely a redirect.
     Same-host URLs only (protocol requirement, and asserted for the INDEX by
     `test_every_sitemap_index_loc_is_on_the_indexes_own_host`); discovered via robots.txt.
     welcome.html and invite-accept.html are auth-gated (noindex) and intentionally
     omitted. /auth lives on the app origin (app.premiselabs.co) since #4054, so it is
     not a URL of this sitemap either. -->
